1
00:00:39,500 --> 00:00:42,940
Something will work out, I'm sure.

2
00:00:55,920 --> 00:00:59,920
Anyone without a job, come to me.

3
00:00:59,920 --> 00:01:04,520
I don't have any either, so don't worry.

4
00:01:04,520 --> 00:01:11,960
Look, even Akaneru is burning up.

5
00:01:13,560 --> 00:01:18,260
Something will work out eventually.

6
00:01:20,380 --> 00:01:23,520
You understand, right?
I understand, I understand.

7
00:01:23,520 --> 00:01:27,460
Once you understand, shut up and follow me.

8
00:01:41,200 --> 00:01:42,860
Did you need something from me?

9
00:01:44,060 --> 00:01:45,760
Even just one month's worth is fine.

10
00:01:45,760 --> 00:01:48,040
I was thinking you could pay off your tab.

11
00:01:49,860 --> 00:01:50,740
I see.

12
00:01:51,960 --> 00:01:52,840
Now, maybe?

13
00:01:52,840 --> 00:01:55,140
Yes, right now.

14
00:01:56,920 --> 00:01:57,800
Well, well.

15
00:01:59,300 --> 00:02:01,340
Where are you going, Ryo-san?

16
00:02:02,560 --> 00:02:07,360
No, my body's been quiet lately,
so I thought I'd do some exercises.

17
00:02:07,880 --> 00:02:10,200
Just because we're neighbors,
if you take me too lightly,

18
00:02:10,200 --> 00:02:12,620
in the end I'll take this to the authorities,
Ryo-san.

19
00:02:12,620 --> 00:02:15,380
I never said I wouldn't pay, did I?

20
00:02:15,380 --> 00:02:17,520
Probably around my next bonus.

21
00:02:18,120 --> 00:02:20,160
Do you expect me to believe that nonsense?

22
00:02:20,160 --> 00:02:23,100
Let's go to the bank right now.
Pay up right now.

23
00:02:23,100 --> 00:02:24,680
Well, right now...

24
00:02:28,680 --> 00:02:29,480
Well, then

25
00:02:32,860 --> 00:02:36,060
That's a horse racing ticket, isn't it?

26
00:02:36,060 --> 00:02:38,940
Sure, it's a betting ticket,
but what a ticket!

27
00:02:38,940 --> 00:02:41,800
The horses I bought on a fluke,
ranked ninth and tenth in popularity,

28
00:02:41,800 --> 00:02:45,020
miraculously finished one-two, a quinella!

29
00:02:45,020 --> 00:02:47,480
a huge long-shot, 30,000-yen ticket.

30
00:02:48,280 --> 00:02:49,780
30,000 yen?

31
00:02:50,740 --> 00:02:52,740
So, how much did you bet?

32
00:02:52,960 --> 00:02:54,420
10,000 yen.

33
00:02:54,420 --> 00:02:56,000
10,000 yen?

34
00:02:56,220 --> 00:02:59,900
Let's see, 10,000 yen times 300...

35
00:03:01,800 --> 00:03:07,960
Once I cash this in, I'll pay back every
penny I owe and still have change left over.

36
00:03:07,960 --> 00:03:13,140
Well, don't get seasick, and just
wait like you're on the Treasure Ship.

37
00:03:13,960 --> 00:03:16,620
Alright, then cash it in right away.

38
00:03:16,620 --> 00:03:20,640
Yeah, yeah, yeah,
but today the holding cell is closed,

39
00:03:20,640 --> 00:03:22,000
Excuse me, officer.

40
00:03:24,020 --> 00:03:25,500
I have something I'd
like to consult you about.

41
00:03:25,500 --> 00:03:28,760
What consultation? What is it?

42
00:03:28,760 --> 00:03:30,120
Well, actually...

43
00:03:31,340 --> 00:03:32,540
That's terrible.

44
00:03:32,820 --> 00:03:36,420
Well, then, I have duties at the main building,
so I'll take my leave.

45
00:03:36,620 --> 00:03:38,160
Let's go, let's go.

46
00:03:41,460 --> 00:03:45,060
Tricked into going to Kameari,
and then to Narita.

47
00:03:49,640 --> 00:03:51,860
Kazumi Haruyama, 25 years old.

48
00:03:52,260 --> 00:03:52,955
A few days ago,

49
00:03:53,005 --> 00:03:56,920
she lent train fare to someone
in trouble at Kameari Station.

50
00:03:57,160 --> 00:03:58,400
So, how much did she lend?

51
00:03:59,120 --> 00:04:00,020
3,000 yen.

52
00:04:00,020 --> 00:04:03,660
She was told they'd definitely pay it back,
so she gave her contact info too.

53
00:04:03,660 --> 00:04:04,220
And?

54
00:04:04,960 --> 00:04:09,100
Still no word today,
so she called the number they gave her,

55
00:04:09,100 --> 00:04:10,880
and it didn't go through.

56
00:04:10,880 --> 00:04:11,080
Yes.

57
00:04:11,080 --> 00:04:13,500
That's a classic petty loan scam.

58
00:04:13,500 --> 00:04:14,240
Scam?

59
00:04:14,540 --> 00:04:16,240
If you're getting taken
in by that kind of trick,

60
00:04:16,240 --> 00:04:18,880
you won't survive in this harsh world.

61
00:04:18,880 --> 00:04:19,980
Get your act together.

62
00:04:20,980 --> 00:04:23,360
It's not your fault, Haruyama-san.

63
00:04:23,360 --> 00:04:26,180
The one who takes advantage of
someone's kindness is the one at fault.

64
00:04:27,120 --> 00:04:27,700
Here you go.

65
00:04:28,400 --> 00:04:28,680
Thank you very much.

66
00:04:29,780 --> 00:04:33,880
Truth be told, I was often taken
in like that when I was young.

67
00:04:34,440 --> 00:04:35,180
Is that so?

68
00:04:35,180 --> 00:04:38,440
But I never had any money to lend, either.

69
00:04:38,440 --> 00:04:39,480
Ahahaha!

70
00:04:40,300 --> 00:04:43,480
So we're a pair of suckers, then.
Terai, take over for me.

71
00:04:45,040 --> 00:04:48,820
If I don't study up on horses,
I'll just end up a total fool.

72
00:04:48,820 --> 00:04:49,700
Got it.

73
00:04:50,120 --> 00:04:54,820
Actually, I'm about to leave
to compete in a contest gathering violinists from around the world.

74
00:04:54,820 --> 00:04:57,480
for Vienna right now.

75
00:04:58,400 --> 00:04:59,180
A contest in Vienna?

76
00:04:59,840 --> 00:05:00,200
Yes.

77
00:05:00,780 --> 00:05:02,360
Hey, Ryo-san, did you hear?

78
00:05:02,880 --> 00:05:04,780
Let's bet everything on the final race here.

79
00:05:04,780 --> 00:05:06,120
Did you say something?

80
00:05:06,660 --> 00:05:09,460
I think it's probably in that newspaper too.

81
00:05:09,900 --> 00:05:10,260
Really?

82
00:05:11,620 --> 00:05:13,640
Ryo-san, lend me the newspaper for a sec.

83
00:05:13,640 --> 00:05:16,060
What are you doing? Ugh, honestly.

84
00:05:16,060 --> 00:05:17,640
Leave the racing page behind.

85
00:05:19,060 --> 00:05:20,860
Found it. Right there.

86
00:05:20,860 --> 00:05:23,540
Rookie violinist Tō Ryūmon

87
00:05:23,540 --> 00:05:25,620
the International Violin Competition

88
00:05:25,620 --> 00:05:27,920
is being held in Vienna
the day after tomorrow.

89
00:05:28,400 --> 00:05:33,440
Japan's favorite to win, 25-year-old
Kazumi Haruyama, is scheduled to compete.

90
00:05:34,240 --> 00:05:36,680
Haruyama Kazumi? It's the same person!

91
00:05:36,680 --> 00:05:39,260
Wow, we met a celebrity, Ryo-san!

92
00:05:39,260 --> 00:05:41,100
Could I get a handshake, please?

93
00:05:41,100 --> 00:05:44,900
No, calling me famous...
I'm still just a beginner.

94
00:05:44,900 --> 00:05:45,680
Let's see, let's see.

95
00:05:45,680 --> 00:05:50,380
By the way, the first-place prize
for this competition is 10 million yen.

96
00:05:50,380 --> 00:05:52,980
10 million yen? Is that true?

97
00:05:54,440 --> 00:05:57,080
Must be nice being so talented.

98
00:05:58,400 --> 00:05:59,420
Hey, phone call, Terai.

99
00:05:59,620 --> 00:05:59,900
Mm.

100
00:06:00,880 --> 00:06:04,740
So in other words,
you're expected to win the championship.

101
00:06:05,400 --> 00:06:07,598
Yes, the pre-race buzz is high.

102
00:06:07,648 --> 00:06:10,540
Some people even say it's a sure win.

103
00:06:10,960 --> 00:06:13,550
If it's a sure win,

104
00:06:13,600 --> 00:06:16,720
that makes you the double-circle favorite

105
00:06:16,960 --> 00:06:17,740
Favorite horse?

106
00:06:17,840 --> 00:06:19,548
If you were a racehorse,

107
00:06:19,598 --> 00:06:22,060
I'd bet my entire fortune on you right now.

108
00:06:23,340 --> 00:06:24,460
Yes, understood.

109
00:06:24,940 --> 00:06:29,960
Hey, Ryo-san, I heard an old woman dropped
her wallet down a drain on Third Street.

110
00:06:29,960 --> 00:06:31,920
I'm going to go check it out for a bit.

111
00:06:31,920 --> 00:06:33,560
Go on, go on.

112
00:06:33,560 --> 00:06:35,660
Leave the ten million to me.

113
00:06:35,660 --> 00:06:36,740
Ten million?

114
00:06:37,240 --> 00:06:39,160
Well then, good luck out there.

115
00:06:39,160 --> 00:06:39,500
Yes.

116
00:06:40,460 --> 00:06:41,400
Well, I'm off.

117
00:06:43,280 --> 00:06:45,020
Well, I should get going too.

118
00:06:45,020 --> 00:06:46,380
You're leaving already?

119
00:06:46,820 --> 00:06:48,560
Yes, thank you very much.

120
00:06:49,760 --> 00:06:52,080
But we're still talking about the ten million,
you know.

121
00:06:55,140 --> 00:06:55,860
It's gone.

122
00:06:55,860 --> 00:06:56,720
What's wrong?

123
00:06:57,300 --> 00:06:58,840
My wallet is missing.

124
00:06:58,840 --> 00:07:00,780
What? Look harder.

125
00:07:00,780 --> 00:07:02,460
You must have tucked it away somewhere.

126
00:07:04,540 --> 00:07:08,500
My wallet had all my money and
my plane ticket to Vienna in it.

127
00:07:09,800 --> 00:07:10,160
It's not here.

128
00:07:10,540 --> 00:07:11,320
Let me see.

129
00:07:14,240 --> 00:07:15,280
Without that...

130
00:07:16,120 --> 00:07:16,780
Please.

131
00:07:16,780 --> 00:07:20,120
Please lend me money for my trip to Vienna.

132
00:07:20,120 --> 00:07:20,980
What?

133
00:07:22,080 --> 00:07:30,280
If I win the competition and get the prize money, I'll pay you back double...
no, triple. But right now, unfortunately, I don't have any cash on hand.

134
00:07:30,280 --> 00:07:38,460
Even if you don't have cash, say you happen to have a winning betting ticket...
a winning ticket... No, how did you know that?

135
00:07:38,460 --> 00:07:45,040
Sorry about that.
Never mind. Is it near here?

136
00:07:45,040 --> 00:07:47,360
Why don't you borrow money from your family?

137
00:07:47,360 --> 00:07:50,760
I haven't seen my
parents back home in years.

138
00:07:51,520 --> 00:07:54,160
My father is a businessman who
runs several companies, but...

139
00:07:54,660 --> 00:07:56,900
He got angry when I started playing
the violin and things like that.

140
00:07:57,840 --> 00:07:58,980
I was disowned.

141
00:08:00,140 --> 00:08:03,400
Besides,
I spent every day practicing the violin,

142
00:08:03,960 --> 00:08:05,140
and I have no friends either.

143
00:08:05,500 --> 00:08:07,900
I suppose I have no choice but to give up.

144
00:08:08,560 --> 00:08:09,160
Give up on what?

145
00:08:09,160 --> 00:08:10,140
The competition.

146
00:08:10,140 --> 00:08:12,160
Give up?

147
00:08:12,160 --> 00:08:16,520
You're the sure-fire top pick to win,
and you'd get ten million yen!

148
00:08:18,140 --> 00:08:20,740
But I need the money, you know.

149
00:08:21,220 --> 00:08:24,840
So what happens to the ten
million yen prize in that case?

150
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:28,880
Naturally,
it goes into someone else's hands.

151
00:08:31,580 --> 00:08:34,720
Oh no, it's ten million, ten million!

152
00:08:34,720 --> 00:08:37,820
And it's right within reach!

153
00:08:37,820 --> 00:08:42,440
Where's the idiot who doesn't buy a ticket for
a race when the winning horse is already known?

154
00:08:47,520 --> 00:08:49,040
Alright, leave it to me!

155
00:08:50,500 --> 00:08:52,820
So you'll lend me the travel money, right?

156
00:08:56,680 --> 00:08:59,380
Phew, I finally found my wallet.

157
00:08:59,900 --> 00:09:00,580
I'm back.

158
00:09:01,200 --> 00:09:03,500
Terai-san, welcome back.

159
00:09:04,160 --> 00:09:05,380
A new wanted poster?

160
00:09:05,860 --> 00:09:06,220
Yes.

161
00:09:07,820 --> 00:09:09,100
I feel like I've seen him somewhere.

162
00:09:12,340 --> 00:09:13,140
Whoa!

163
00:09:15,760 --> 00:09:18,200
It's definitely Hariyama, isn't it, Terai?

164
00:09:18,860 --> 00:09:21,340
Yes, I'm sorry for letting him get away.

165
00:09:21,340 --> 00:09:25,080
The wanted notice only went out after noon,
so it couldn't be helped.

166
00:09:25,080 --> 00:09:29,280
Impersonating a real person
is such a despicable method.

167
00:09:29,880 --> 00:09:34,200
But what does it mean that Ryotsu
disappeared along with Hariyama?

168
00:09:34,580 --> 00:09:38,120
Did Ryotsu know that he
was a wanted con artist?

169
00:09:38,660 --> 00:09:39,800
I don't think so.

170
00:09:40,300 --> 00:09:43,220
Don't tell me Ryo-chan
became the scammer's target...

171
00:09:44,920 --> 00:09:45,640
No, no.

172
00:09:46,240 --> 00:09:46,960
Right?

173
00:09:47,620 --> 00:09:51,220
Ryotsu's got debts but no savings, you know.

174
00:09:51,220 --> 00:09:52,860
Is Ryo-san in?

175
00:09:54,380 --> 00:09:55,920
Well, if it isn't the shopping street folks.

176
00:09:56,620 --> 00:10:00,100
Ryotsu's out, but what's going on this time?

177
00:10:00,100 --> 00:10:04,620
Well, you see, we heard Ryo-san hit
it big at the races for 3 million yen.

178
00:10:04,620 --> 00:10:06,740
We came for this month's collection.

179
00:10:08,320 --> 00:10:12,360
Ryotsu won 3 million yen at the races?

180
00:10:12,600 --> 00:10:14,780
Yes... but if he's not here, never mind.

181
00:10:15,180 --> 00:10:17,500
He wouldn't skip town, would he?

182
00:10:17,500 --> 00:10:18,400
Well, thanks.

183
00:10:20,300 --> 00:10:21,100
3 million

184
00:10:21,100 --> 00:10:26,300
Ryo-san, you never mentioned to me
that you hit 3 million at the races.

185
00:10:26,720 --> 00:10:30,660
Can someone explain what
on earth is going on?

186
00:10:30,660 --> 00:10:31,960
Chief.

187
00:10:32,860 --> 00:10:37,080
So what that means is Hariyama,
who was looking for a sucker,

188
00:10:38,020 --> 00:10:40,720
Yes! 10,000 yen turned into 3 million yen!

189
00:10:41,360 --> 00:10:46,940
spotted a senior who happened to hit 3 million
yen at the races and set his sights on him.

190
00:10:48,240 --> 00:10:50,060
This much is fine, right?

191
00:10:50,460 --> 00:10:50,860
Yeah.

192
00:10:50,860 --> 00:10:54,640
But would that senior really
get fooled by a con artist?

193
00:10:56,460 --> 00:10:57,180
No, no.

194
00:10:57,980 --> 00:11:00,580
Where are we going?

195
00:11:00,580 --> 00:11:03,580
What? What did you say?

196
00:11:04,040 --> 00:11:07,020
We're going to cash in the
big winning ticket, right?

197
00:11:08,480 --> 00:11:09,400
What?

198
00:11:10,520 --> 00:11:11,240
That's why -

199
00:11:12,520 --> 00:11:13,220
I see.

200
00:11:13,660 --> 00:11:16,760
I think big winning tickets can
only be cashed in at the racetrack.

201
00:11:17,420 --> 00:11:19,720
That's why we're heading
to Nakayama Racecourse.

202
00:11:25,180 --> 00:11:27,120
The racecourse is that way, over there.

203
00:11:27,120 --> 00:11:30,600
Don't worry,
I'll take you all the way to Narita Airport.

204
00:11:32,380 --> 00:11:34,260
Why, why Narita?

205
00:11:46,980 --> 00:11:47,780
Stop the car.

206
00:11:49,720 --> 00:11:53,320
Who knows how many hours it'll take
to get to Narita from the office?

207
00:11:53,320 --> 00:11:55,180
Don't whine like that.

208
00:11:55,180 --> 00:11:58,400
At this rate,
you'll never win the competition.

209
00:11:59,320 --> 00:12:01,020
And about my fee.

210
00:12:01,020 --> 00:12:02,940
I'd normally take seventy-thirty,

211
00:12:02,940 --> 00:12:05,920
but I'll cut it down to just
ten percent of the prize money.

212
00:12:05,920 --> 00:12:08,400
Just make sure you don't forget that.

213
00:12:08,400 --> 00:12:11,500
How did it come to this?

214
00:12:11,960 --> 00:12:13,080
Something's wrong here.

215
00:12:13,560 --> 00:12:15,180
In that case, we change the plan.

216
00:12:15,180 --> 00:12:17,300
I'll steal the winning
ticket when no one's looking.

217
00:12:17,300 --> 00:12:18,160
Alright!

218
00:12:20,000 --> 00:12:35,180
Ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow
ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow

219
00:12:35,180 --> 00:12:37,940
Don't be so dramatic,
just from skipping one meal.

220
00:12:39,040 --> 00:12:40,060
I can't go on.

221
00:12:40,060 --> 00:12:43,500
Hey, Haruyama, pull yourself together!

222
00:12:45,120 --> 00:12:46,460
Well, there's no helping it.

223
00:12:46,960 --> 00:12:47,400
Right.

224
00:12:48,720 --> 00:12:49,860
Wait here a moment.

225
00:12:53,440 --> 00:12:53,880
What?

226
00:12:54,940 --> 00:12:57,420
What on earth are you doing?

227
00:12:57,420 --> 00:13:00,320
Edible weeds grow even in places like this,
you know.

228
00:13:01,960 --> 00:13:03,020
Come on, eat up.

229
00:13:04,300 --> 00:13:06,360
There's no way I can eat that!

230
00:13:06,360 --> 00:13:08,200
Come on, don't be shy.

231
00:13:08,200 --> 00:13:09,260
No thanks.

232
00:13:09,260 --> 00:13:11,480
Please stop.

233
00:13:11,480 --> 00:13:14,200
Try it, it's delicious!

234
00:13:14,200 --> 00:13:17,380
Stop it, I'm not a horse!

235
00:13:17,980 --> 00:13:21,240
What on earth will you do if you
eat that and get an upset stomach?

236
00:13:22,560 --> 00:13:23,840
I see.

237
00:13:23,840 --> 00:13:27,920
If you get a stomachache
and can't compete in the race,

238
00:13:27,920 --> 00:13:30,480
the ten million yen prize goes down the drain,
doesn't it?

239
00:13:30,480 --> 00:13:32,340
Whew, that was close.

240
00:13:33,160 --> 00:13:34,040
Did you eat it?

241
00:13:34,340 --> 00:13:37,400
If this girl wins the competition,

242
00:13:38,380 --> 00:13:41,020
first there's the ten
million yen winner's prize,

243
00:13:41,020 --> 00:13:44,740
plus solo concerts and commercials.

244
00:13:45,520 --> 00:13:47,620
They'll protect my precious shoulder.

245
00:13:47,620 --> 00:13:49,480
Hatte Sukkiri Petarinkon

246
00:13:49,480 --> 00:13:52,960
Plus, appearances in
movies and variety shows,

247
00:13:52,960 --> 00:13:57,900
photo books, instructional books,
autobiographies, and so on.

248
00:13:58,620 --> 00:14:01,400
The economic impact would be incalculable.

249
00:14:03,060 --> 00:14:04,913
If you ever run into any trouble,

250
00:14:04,963 --> 00:14:07,160
I'll always be here to help you out.

251
00:14:07,320 --> 00:14:09,080
Just like a Bin-Wan manager.

252
00:14:09,300 --> 00:14:13,080
If you want, let's put a management
agreement in writing right here.

253
00:14:13,340 --> 00:14:15,740
What's this old geezer going on about?

254
00:14:16,080 --> 00:14:19,000
Damn it, we just have to hold on
until we get that big winning ticket.

255
00:14:19,600 --> 00:14:21,140
I look forward to working with you then.

256
00:14:23,540 --> 00:14:25,520
Alright, I'll get you something to eat.

257
00:14:30,540 --> 00:14:33,180
Yes, chew well and eat slowly.

258
00:14:33,180 --> 00:14:34,040
Thanks.

259
00:14:37,060 --> 00:14:39,560
You said you'd feed me,
and it's just one rice ball?

260
00:14:41,620 --> 00:14:44,320
Hey, do you even know how to wrap the nori?

261
00:14:44,320 --> 00:14:47,020
You know, the one where you pull it
out from the bottom in one quick motion.

262
00:14:49,140 --> 00:14:53,480
Now, just pull this plastic here
and the rice ball comes right out.

263
00:14:55,140 --> 00:14:56,960
Even a brat knows that much.

264
00:14:57,680 --> 00:15:00,320
Just what you'd expect
from a sheltered artist.

265
00:15:00,320 --> 00:15:01,700
Victory is guaranteed.

266
00:15:01,700 --> 00:15:04,460
Come on, don't hold back. Eat, eat.

267
00:15:06,220 --> 00:15:09,200
You won 3 million yen and you're still this stingy,
you old geezer.

268
00:15:09,920 --> 00:15:12,740
This is what they mean by
catching a sea bream with a shrimp.

269
00:15:14,040 --> 00:15:16,380
And on top of that, you're incredibly dense.

270
00:15:17,080 --> 00:15:18,820
If it comes to this,
we'll have to use force.

271
00:15:19,180 --> 00:15:21,160
Why should we wait meekly

272
00:15:21,160 --> 00:15:22,580
for the other side to hand
over a big winning ticket?

273
00:15:23,540 --> 00:15:26,040
Good things come to those who wait...
and so do hand warmers.

274
00:15:27,720 --> 00:15:29,520
That spot there is dirty.

275
00:15:29,520 --> 00:15:30,660
Hm? Where?

276
00:15:31,540 --> 00:15:33,880
No, not that one, the dress shirt.

277
00:15:33,880 --> 00:15:34,760
Where?

278
00:15:35,100 --> 00:15:36,740
Then please take off your shirt.

279
00:15:37,620 --> 00:15:40,240
I'll go wash it at the
convenience store's tap.

280
00:15:41,000 --> 00:15:42,420
Thanks. Sorry about that.

281
00:15:42,820 --> 00:15:45,220
I was just thinking it was
about time to do the laundry.

282
00:15:45,220 --> 00:15:48,440
I've been wearing this for about two months straight,
you know.

283
00:15:48,440 --> 00:15:51,700
With weather like this,
a dress shirt will dry in no time.

284
00:15:54,360 --> 00:15:56,820
Right, I'll wipe off the stain
on your jacket while I'm at it.

285
00:15:56,820 --> 00:15:58,180
Thanks.

286
00:15:58,180 --> 00:16:00,760
No problem, easy.

287
00:16:01,920 --> 00:16:03,100
Well, I'm off.

288
00:16:03,100 --> 00:16:07,940
It's just a betting ticket.

289
00:16:09,240 --> 00:16:10,380
When did that get there?

290
00:16:10,880 --> 00:16:12,920
Hurry up, we don't have much time!

291
00:16:13,620 --> 00:16:14,420
Right.

292
00:16:14,420 --> 00:16:17,240
Damn it, without the betting ticket,
this is useless.

293
00:16:17,680 --> 00:16:18,640
Over here.

294
00:16:23,460 --> 00:16:26,820
Thanks to you,
my shirt's cold and feels great, Hariyama!

295
00:16:27,860 --> 00:16:29,280
Well, I'm glad to hear that.

296
00:16:31,620 --> 00:16:37,220
Damn, eating weeds just made me even hungrier.
Just kidding. Tasty, thanks.

297
00:16:37,220 --> 00:16:39,740
It's not funny at all, seriously.

298
00:16:39,740 --> 00:16:41,960
You might as well become the horse yourself!

299
00:16:42,480 --> 00:16:44,400
What's wrong?

300
00:16:45,020 --> 00:16:45,920
Nothing.

301
00:16:46,900 --> 00:16:48,180
Alright, one more try.

302
00:16:49,280 --> 00:16:51,320
Wait, I was sure the betting
ticket was right here a second ago.

303
00:16:52,880 --> 00:16:54,840
Was it up front?

304
00:16:56,700 --> 00:16:58,440
Hey! What are you doing?!

305
00:16:58,640 --> 00:16:59,560
Stop it!

306
00:16:59,580 --> 00:17:00,660
I didn't do anything!

307
00:17:00,820 --> 00:17:01,380
You!

308
00:17:02,860 --> 00:17:06,420
Ow!

309
00:17:08,500 --> 00:17:10,440
Ugh... ow

310
00:17:10,900 --> 00:17:12,020
Did you get hurt?

311
00:17:12,820 --> 00:17:14,000
Ah ah ah

312
00:17:14,000 --> 00:17:15,860
Looks like just a scratch to me.

313
00:17:15,860 --> 00:17:19,060
Something like this heals
right up if you just spit on it.

314
00:17:19,060 --> 00:17:19,480
Hey.

315
00:17:19,480 --> 00:17:22,000
Whoa! H-hey, what are you doing?!

316
00:17:23,280 --> 00:17:24,420
See, you can still run just fine.

317
00:17:24,980 --> 00:17:26,860
Looks like you're not hurt anywhere else.

318
00:17:27,320 --> 00:17:30,060
More importantly,
is your precious tool of the trade safe?

319
00:17:30,300 --> 00:17:31,460
Tool of the trade?

320
00:17:34,360 --> 00:17:35,280
I'm fine.

321
00:17:36,140 --> 00:17:38,620
I see. Looks like this
one's badly hurt, then.

322
00:17:49,600 --> 00:17:50,460
I can't take it anymore.

323
00:17:51,600 --> 00:17:53,980
Okay, this should get us running somehow.

324
00:17:53,980 --> 00:17:55,020
Let's go.

325
00:17:55,900 --> 00:17:59,120
No way, it's pointless to keep going.
Let's just go home.

326
00:18:01,340 --> 00:18:03,100
Wait, just leave me alone already.

327
00:18:03,920 --> 00:18:06,220
What's gotten into you all of a sudden,
Hariyama?

328
00:18:06,820 --> 00:18:11,540
Hariyama? I'm not Hariyama.

329
00:18:11,540 --> 00:18:12,240
What?

330
00:18:13,140 --> 00:18:17,380
I'm not a violinist,
a pianist, or even an exorcist.

331
00:18:17,380 --> 00:18:20,220
Shane! That's why I'm going back to Tokyo!

332
00:18:22,060 --> 00:18:22,700
Harayama?

333
00:18:23,380 --> 00:18:26,120
I already told you, I'm not Harayama!

334
00:18:27,220 --> 00:18:28,540
Hey, hold on! What are you doing?

335
00:18:28,640 --> 00:18:30,440
What on earth is going on?!

336
00:18:30,580 --> 00:18:31,980
Ow ow ow I give up!

337
00:18:32,100 --> 00:18:33,460
I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

338
00:18:33,580 --> 00:18:35,200
I won't do it again! I'm sorry!

339
00:18:35,500 --> 00:18:36,520
Sorry!

340
00:18:38,320 --> 00:18:39,420
You damn idiot old man!

341
00:18:39,680 --> 00:18:40,000
What?

342
00:18:41,740 --> 00:18:42,520
No way! No way! No way!

343
00:18:43,000 --> 00:18:44,840
What's wrong with you? Calm down!

344
00:18:44,840 --> 00:18:46,800
Take a deep breath. Deep breath.

345
00:18:51,940 --> 00:18:54,580
Nothing's going right for me lately.

346
00:18:55,040 --> 00:18:57,640
I get stuck with some weird old geezer,
and it's already freezing.

347
00:18:57,640 --> 00:19:01,200
What a pain.

348
00:19:01,200 --> 00:19:02,860
I don't care anymore.

349
00:19:03,380 --> 00:19:05,200
It pisses me off, damn it.

350
00:19:11,800 --> 00:19:13,180
Don't worry.

351
00:19:15,840 --> 00:19:18,360
Even if God has abandoned you,

352
00:19:18,360 --> 00:19:20,880
I'm still on your side.

353
00:19:27,940 --> 00:19:30,420
Don't worry, you can do it if you try.

354
00:19:33,080 --> 00:19:34,780
Relax.

355
00:19:34,780 --> 00:19:38,380
Use the talent heaven gave you
and all your strength

356
00:19:38,380 --> 00:19:40,960
and go show it off fully in Vienna.

357
00:19:40,960 --> 00:19:41,820
Hariyama!

358
00:19:46,680 --> 00:19:50,040
Once you've decided to do something,
don't just give up on it so easily.

359
00:19:50,040 --> 00:19:51,060
Got it?

360
00:19:51,480 --> 00:19:52,220
Understand?

361
00:19:52,220 --> 00:19:52,860
Yes.

362
00:19:52,860 --> 00:19:54,100
Alright then.

363
00:19:56,780 --> 00:20:00,920
I'm definitely, absolutely, positively going
to snatch that jackpot ticket from this guy.

364
00:20:11,960 --> 00:20:12,680
Watch out!

365
00:20:16,200 --> 00:20:17,620
Where's the flight to Vienna?

366
00:20:17,620 --> 00:20:18,680
The flight to Vienna...

367
00:20:20,480 --> 00:20:23,340
Which airline would you like to use?

368
00:20:23,340 --> 00:20:24,200
Where is it?

369
00:20:25,020 --> 00:20:25,920
Um...

370
00:20:25,920 --> 00:20:27,480
Over there... no, I think it's this way.

371
00:20:27,480 --> 00:20:28,420
Get it together.

372
00:20:30,060 --> 00:20:31,320
Anyway, it's Vienna.

373
00:20:31,320 --> 00:20:33,340
Quickly look it up on that terminal.

374
00:20:33,340 --> 00:20:35,640
The reservation name is in this article.

375
00:20:35,640 --> 00:20:37,020
For Hariyama.

376
00:20:37,020 --> 00:20:38,760
I won't let you go to Vienna.

377
00:20:40,260 --> 00:20:41,940
H-how did you find me here?

378
00:20:42,680 --> 00:20:47,247
You were planning to skip town with the 3 million from that long-shot ticket,
weren't you?

379
00:20:47,297 --> 00:20:48,520
Not so fast.

380
00:20:48,780 --> 00:20:50,220
N-no way...

381
00:20:50,920 --> 00:20:51,780
Mr. Hariyama.

382
00:20:53,600 --> 00:20:57,560
Kazumi Harayama, could you give us
your honest impressions right now?

383
00:20:59,080 --> 00:21:00,820
I'm very nervous.

384
00:21:01,160 --> 00:21:02,268
Kazumi Harayama,

385
00:21:02,318 --> 00:21:06,620
my confidence in winning the contest is just to do my best,
isn't it?

386
00:21:07,140 --> 00:21:07,920
Harayama?

387
00:21:08,400 --> 00:21:10,480
You... wait a moment.

388
00:21:10,480 --> 00:21:12,700
Hey! Hey! Who are you?

389
00:21:13,300 --> 00:21:16,980
Heh! I'm a con man after the big payout!

390
00:21:17,160 --> 00:21:17,760
What?

391
00:21:18,060 --> 00:21:19,980
It's rakugo storyteller Hayashiya Kobuhei!

392
00:21:20,060 --> 00:21:21,200
Where? Where's Kobuhei?

393
00:21:21,420 --> 00:21:22,500
Kobuhei went that way!

394
00:21:22,500 --> 00:21:23,940
Look, it's Kobuhei! Kobuhei!

395
00:21:24,100 --> 00:21:24,560
There he is!

396
00:21:26,080 --> 00:21:28,140
Sorry! We're taking this betting ticket!

397
00:21:29,680 --> 00:21:31,220
Ryo-san! Are you all right?

398
00:21:31,700 --> 00:21:33,700
Damn it! Wait!

399
00:21:35,100 --> 00:21:37,440
Running away again?
He's been doing it since earlier!

400
00:21:37,780 --> 00:21:39,580
W-wait!

401
00:21:40,480 --> 00:21:41,100
Wait!

402
00:21:42,900 --> 00:21:43,840
Wait!

403
00:21:43,840 --> 00:21:43,920
Wait!

404
00:21:45,320 --> 00:21:46,300
Yaah!

405
00:21:46,380 --> 00:21:47,180
Bam!

406
00:21:47,180 --> 00:21:48,800
Take this!

407
00:21:49,780 --> 00:21:52,060
How dare you deceive us!

408
00:21:52,060 --> 00:21:53,140
Gaga gaga gaga gaga

409
00:21:53,140 --> 00:21:54,600
Ryo-san, that's enough, right?

410
00:21:54,680 --> 00:21:57,680
Let's have that betting
ticket handed over here.

411
00:21:58,420 --> 00:21:59,180
Well?

412
00:21:59,180 --> 00:22:01,280
The betting ticket

413
00:22:01,280 --> 00:22:02,780
Come on, hand it over!

414
00:22:02,860 --> 00:22:03,120
Gaga

415
00:22:03,120 --> 00:22:04,460
Here you go!

416
00:22:07,920 --> 00:22:09,340
Unusually obedient, aren't you?

417
00:22:10,520 --> 00:22:13,180
People should be a little contrary now and then,
shouldn't they?

418
00:22:13,740 --> 00:22:17,240
Exactly, Ryo-san,
you're finally becoming a normal person.

419
00:22:17,240 --> 00:22:19,320
You really did hit it, right?

420
00:22:19,880 --> 00:22:21,340
Maybe it's a losing ticket.

421
00:22:24,520 --> 00:22:25,540
No way.

422
00:22:30,040 --> 00:22:31,200
The Takarazuka Kinen?

423
00:22:34,360 --> 00:22:35,360
The Takarazuka Kinen?

424
00:22:35,600 --> 00:22:37,420
That was over four months ago!

425
00:22:37,940 --> 00:22:39,460
Con man, keep quiet.

426
00:22:40,480 --> 00:22:41,820
The Takarazuka Kinen entry...

427
00:22:41,820 --> 00:22:46,460
Sixty days' grace.

428
00:22:46,460 --> 00:22:49,680
Then it's a losing ticket after all

429
00:22:52,160 --> 00:22:54,520
You tricked us! You tricked us!

430
00:22:54,520 --> 00:23:01,960
Grandpa, back in the day you had losing tickets in your pocket too Yeah,
that kind of thing happens, hehe.

431
00:23:08,060 --> 00:23:10,480
Station all officers at every exit!

432
00:23:10,480 --> 00:23:11,420
Hurry!

433
00:23:16,980 --> 00:23:17,700
There he is!

434
00:23:18,220 --> 00:23:19,260
Crazy!

435
00:23:19,260 --> 00:23:21,380
Everyone, stay calm.

436
00:23:21,920 --> 00:23:27,260
As expected of Ryo-san.

437
00:23:27,260 --> 00:23:29,160
He must be talking the suspect down.

438
00:23:29,160 --> 00:23:30,380
Doesn't look like it.

439
00:23:32,200 --> 00:23:35,700
He ran! Why is Ryo-san running away?

440
00:23:35,980 --> 00:23:36,800
Stop it!

441
00:23:37,420 --> 00:23:38,900
Ryo-san!

442
00:23:39,280 --> 00:23:41,160
If you're that suspicious!

443
00:23:41,560 --> 00:23:42,860
You con man!

444
00:23:43,340 --> 00:23:44,100
It's Hariyama!

445
00:23:44,240 --> 00:23:45,180
What? That!

446
00:23:46,180 --> 00:23:48,500
Hey, wait! Are you a con man or what?!

447
00:23:49,220 --> 00:23:52,620
You're one to talk! Pay back the
120 yen I spent on your rice ball!

448
00:23:53,100 --> 00:23:55,000
Pay your tab! Your tab!

449
00:23:55,700 --> 00:23:58,220
I'll pay when my next bonus comes in!

450
00:23:59,320 --> 00:24:00,720
You troublemaker!

451
00:24:18,160 --> 00:24:24,520
On a rainy afternoon,
I walked looking back over my shoulder.

452
00:24:24,520 --> 00:24:27,100
Led along by the hand of the gacha.

453
00:24:28,060 --> 00:24:34,280
That strange feeling I had back then.

454
00:24:34,280 --> 00:24:39,520
So, on the arcade street's tiles,

455
00:24:39,520 --> 00:24:45,200
I tried walking only on the black ones.

456
00:24:47,860 --> 00:24:53,580
Everyone was a child once,
but they've all forgotten.

457
00:24:54,520 --> 00:25:00,920
Pompous politicians and the gloomy
aunties who are a thorn in your side,

458
00:25:01,420 --> 00:25:11,680
Come round that corner,
you'll meet everyone, everyone.

459
00:25:14,120 --> 00:25:16,360
There's a wall over there.

460
00:25:17,540 --> 00:25:19,660
Well, surely there's a wall.

461
00:25:21,100 --> 00:25:24,960
Everyone, come on over to our town!

462
00:25:26,000 --> 00:25:26,440
Thank you.

463
00:25:30,200 --> 00:25:32,720
November 11th is Battery Day?

464
00:25:32,860 --> 00:25:36,240
Right, written in kanji it
does look like plus and minus.

465
00:25:36,240 --> 00:25:40,160
So to mark that Battery Day, an
energy-saving house contest is being held?

466
00:25:41,680 --> 00:25:44,120
We'll save energy like crazy
to win the luxury prizes!

467
00:25:44,480 --> 00:25:47,660
See you at the next
energy-saving house showdown!

468
00:25:56,180 --> 00:25:56,500
Thank you.

